      "closure_rationale": "The existing OwScope is a resource protocol implementing a reversed conditional filter, not a semantic undo log. Actual external counters retain every admitted registration effect across raised errors and cleanup. Publication swaps exclusive owners before old release; the new value is observable during cleanup, but no synchronization or reversal of already published effects is inferred. Actual ow_defer/ow_finish/ow_publish and typed ow_allocator are composed unchanged. Six real allocations exercise publication of three staged resources before releasing three old resources. Callback capacity, nonlocal-exit restrictions and explicit guarded rejection are stated. The jump adapter imports actual early er_run/er_raise and converts status before cleanup without modifying automatic locals in the setjmp-containing function. Six C17 profiles run six anchors, eight compiled controls and six compiling-stub rejections. Independent reversed-list filtering checks2735policy/failure histories through depth4, while341retained/error-mask histories check exact consumption traces. Explicit anchors cover capacity8/9, every failure before registration, callback reentrancy rejection, publication-before-release, stale tickets and final-generation cleanup. Actual OW_MUTANT2/12 distinguish unconditional and FIFO cleanup. The required fallible changed contract is implemented separately: RETAINED stops at the top and preserves earlier dependencies, while RELEASED_ERROR consumes the resource exactly once and records a diagnostic. Real typed allocations remain live across pending recovery. Sealed registration bounds diagnostic count and finite generation never obstructs final cleanup. Unknown release is explicitly outside this three-state contract and needs another authority state. Independent delayed learner work remains unassessed. Bounded author support only."
    },
